# Documentation layout

- Do not create planning, release, agent-brief, or checklist markdown at the
  repository root. Put it under `docs/` using
  `docs/README.md` (directory map).
- Only these four trackers live directly under `docs/`:
  `SSCRE_PLAN.md`, `SSCRE_PROJECT_ANALYSIS.md`,
  `SSCRE_LEARNING_AND_EXECUTION_GUIDE.md`, `SSCRE_SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`.
- Use `docs/internal/` for release prep and private briefs, `docs/reference/`
  for technical specs, `docs/setup/` for environment setup, `docs/phase-1/`,
  `docs/phase-2/`, and `docs/phase-3/` for milestone and workstream material.
- Keep new Phase 2 and Phase 3 filenames in `docs/phase-2/` and `docs/phase-3/`
  (flat folders). Code and benchmarks reference those paths; do not nest phase
  files without updating every reference.
- When adding a notable file under `docs/phase-1/`, `docs/phase-2/`,
  `docs/phase-3/`, or `docs/internal/`, add a row to that folder's `README.md`
  index.
- When closing a Phase 3 workstream plan step or promoting feature cards, update
  in the same pass: [`docs/phase-3/PHASE_3_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`](../docs/phase-3/PHASE_3_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)
  (Status, relevant workstream section, baseline gaps), linked evidence paths,
  and [`docs/phase-3/README.md`](../docs/phase-3/README.md) if new files were
  added. Do not leave the parent plan describing pre-close gaps.
- When moving or renaming docs, search the repo for the old path and update
  links in markdown, Python docstrings, and JSON metadata.
